uffs that he learned about the club  from an ex-fighter who acted tough  and offers to take his place since the  other guy went missing they get  permission to join however the  stipulation is that only yuji will be  allowed to fight  since the boss just doesn't like megumi  already this  kinda works out in their favor since  let's be real when we're talking about  fist fights  yuji is probably more suited for that  situation and i want to take a moment to  acknowledge the change of pace here  it is super welcome we just went through  a ton  of heavy moments especially with maki  and the zenins  so coming back to an infiltration  mission that is basically just fight  club  is a great way to simmer things down and  give us a moment to catch our breath  after all the terrifying things we just  saw especially after a month-long break  where maybe the pacing would have  suffered for it yuji is a little bit  nervous about their bluff being pushed a  bit far  however megami deduces that if there are  cursed users here  then there's probably a lot of  reorganizing going on and they're most  likely safe  not to mention he is fairly certain that  hikari  was already watching them through the  security camera so they must be getting  close to finally meeting him  the gambling club is already distrusting  of megami though so they'll have to be  extra careful the problem is that the  culling game starts in just  nine days and time is running out  because of this megami decides that they  need to make a move  tonight they cannot afford to wait but  he does state that at the first sign of  trouble  they're gonna have to leave they need to  play this very quickly but also  very safe we cut ahead to tyler  explaining the rules to yuji  for the fight club i mean for the  gambling club  very different things and the most  important things  are that the customers are enjoying  themselves as a result the main two  rules in each fight  are that firstly the fighters can't use  jujutsu techniques  after all if the customers can't see  what's happening  there's no point in them even coming it  would be a pretty bad show in that case  i think  secondly there's no running allowed you  need to fight where the customers can  see you  furthermore there are also two kinds of  fights  real fights and scripted ones and most  importantly those scripted matches  are written by the boss meaning that if  yuji wants to meet hikari  the most straightforward way for him to  do so is to put on one hell of a show  and speaking of shows it is officially  time for the fight  to begin as we see this parking lot has  been made into a makeshift arena by  removing the ceiling  to allow for people to watch from the  upper floor and it looks like it's gonna  be a hell of a fight for the spectators  as well as one that we can enjoy because  yuji's first match  is going to be against panda panda  obviously is going through his own  things at this time  but at least for this moment he seems to  be pretty well held together  i had never really even contemplated the  idea of yuji fighting panda because  it never really seemed like it would  make sense for it to happen  but now that it's here i'm pretty  excited by it sure they can't use their  curse techniques but these guys are more  or less physical brawlers anyways  so i can imagine that it's going to be a  pretty good match honestly  people begin placing their bets and we  see this girl with star-shaped pupils  talking to hikari but he just seems  bored with the situation  saying that no one wants to watch a man  fight a panda because the outcome  is predetermined and vets with  guaranteed outcomes are just  kinda lame however in reality the fight  is anything but boring the crowd and  announcers are going wild as yuji and  the panda give  everything they have for a short time  however at this same time  panda is explaining that because he and  hikari have history together  there's no question of why he's there  but even so he's still being avoided  they're having this discussion  while putting on the show and it's great  he goes on to say that there's actually  another third year student whose  technique might be a problem  which is interesting i don't think we've  had any information on this extra third  year  at all up until now however what i do  know is that almost every third year  student we've met so far  is a monster so i'm assuming they will  be too  panda sets yuji up for the victory and  yuji sends him flying  immediately drawing the attention of  hikari who just watched this man beat up  a panda  and watch the arena go electric as a  result he calls someone at the arena and  says that yuji will be winning  all of his fights going forward and that  his way of fighting  was very deliberate towards drawing  attention to the fight  hikari is beyond excited to work with  him saying that he could write a whole  book  worth of scripts for this fighter we  also find out the name of the starry  eyed girl who seems to be the other  third year student that panda was  talking about earlier  with her name being hoshi kirara this is  pretty fitting since hoshi means star  and her eyes have stars in them  but either way as the conversation keeps  going we see megami listening in from  the shadows as they talk about how  kirara will be sent to watch him later  since they still don't trust him and  with that the chapter comes to the close  as hikari says that the last time he  felt like this was when his  ex-girlfriend went on a shopping spree  with his credit cards and he had to take  on  installment payments to pay them off  which i mean i don't know about you but  i'm not usually super happy when i've  had a girlfriend do that  so i'm not sure where this guy really  stands in this situation  maybe he just means that he hasn't been  so fired up or passionate  since that happened because yeah i would  be pretty emotional as well  but we'll have to wait and see like i  said that is all for 